  "final": "I added `ContactStore.find_by_phone(number)` in `contacts/store.py`, and the tests pass.\n\nIt normalizes the query with the same `normalize_phone` that `add` uses, then compares it to the stored numbers. So `4155550100`, `+1 415 555 0100`, `1-415-555-0100` and `415.555.0100` all find the contact stored as `(415) 555-0100`.\n\nIt returns a list of matching contacts, like `find_by_name` does. A number that can't be parsed, such as `\"12\"`, returns an empty list instead of raising `ValueError`.\n\nI added a test for these formats in `tests/test_store.py`.",
